% Facial Prostheses: LCD L33738 and its Policy Article A52463 (DME MACs).
% A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for a facial prosthesis (L8040–L8047, or L8048 for one no code
% describes and for the component attaching it to an implant), for the
% adhesives, remover, wipes and tape used with it (A4364, A4455, A4456,
% A4450, A4452, A5120), or for the materials (L8048) and labor (L8049) of a
% repair or modification is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY. The benefit is not
% durable medical equipment: the Policy Article places facial prostheses
% under the Medicare Artificial Legs, Arms and Eyes benefit of Social
% Security Act §1861(s)(9), so no condition on the place of use applies.
% Skin care products (A9270) are in scope but in no benefit: noncovered.
%
% The coverage criteria:
%   1. loss or absence of facial tissue due to disease, trauma, surgery or a
%      congenital defect — the condition and its cause are facts of the
%      record;
%   2. a replacement — when the previous prosthesis was lost, irreparably
%      damaged or worn, or when a change in the beneficiary's condition
%      cannot be accommodated by modifying it: ONE finding, "replacement
%      justified", whose reasons are these alternatives (the prosthetist's
%      documentation suffices for other than medical reasons, the Article
%      says; a reviewer accepts or rejects it);
%   3. adhesives and tape, and the attachment component, with a covered
%      prosthesis — the item is an accessory of the prosthesis (the shared
%      template);
%   4. a repair — accidental damage or extensive wear that can be repaired
%      (a fact of the record); a modification — more than 90 days after
%      delivery and required by a change in the beneficiary's condition (a
%      judgment: the finding "change in condition requires modification").
%      Both are an accessory of the prosthesis (the shared template, as a
%      shoe modification is of the shoe in therapeutic_shoes.le). What an
%      L8048 claim is for — an unspecified prosthesis, an attachment
%      component, repair materials — is a fact of the record, the kind of
%      the item.
% The ocular component of an orbital, upper facial or hemi-facial
% prosthesis (V2623, V2629), billed by the facial prosthesis supplier, is
% decided by the eye prostheses policy (eye_prostheses.le), not here.
%
% The payment conditions the Article adds (its "Policy specific
% documentation requirements"), in section remedy: for L8048 a description
% of the item in the narrative field of the claim and a drawing or
% photograph available on request; for a replacement fabricated from a new
% impression rather than the previous master model, the reason documented
% in the supplier's records. The same narrative description is required for
% V2629, whose claims the eye prostheses policy decides: not applied there.
%
% Not modelled: the AV, KM, KN, RT and LT modifiers (billing rules); the
% single code for adjacent facial regions and the other coding guidelines
% (an item's code is taken as correct); the jurisdiction of claims for
% implanted components and for prostheses provided in hospital; follow-up
% visits (no code); the unit of service of tape.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* has *a condition* of facial tissue due to *a cause*; undefined.
    the kind of *an item* is *a kind*; undefined.
    *an item* replaces a previous facial prosthesis; undefined.
    *an item* repairs accidental damage or extensive wear to *a device*; undefined.
    *an item* was fabricated from a new impression; undefined.
    the reason for the new impression for *an item* is documented in the supplier records; undefined.
    the claim for *an item* includes a description of the item in the narrative field; undefined.
    a drawing or photograph of *an item* is available; undefined.
    % derived
    *an item* is a facial prosthesis.
    *a beneficiary* has a qualifying facial condition.
    *an item* is a covered facial prosthesis for *a beneficiary*.
    *an item* is used with a covered facial prosthesis.
    *an item* is a repair or modification of a covered facial prosthesis.
    *an item* is a modification made more than 90 days after the delivery of *a device*.
    the narrative description requirement is met for *an item*.
    the photograph requirement is met for *an item*.
    the new impression requirement is met for *an item*.

the knowledge base facial prostheses includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base facial prostheses includes:

LCD L33738 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33738".
the text of LCD L33738 is at "sources/lcd/L33738.txt".
Policy Article A52463 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52463".
the text of Policy Article A52463 is at "sources/article/A52463.txt".

% What a facial prosthesis is: the complete prostheses of the specific
% codes, and an L8048 item that is a prosthesis no code describes.
rule facial_prosthesis_codes with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Codes for a facial prosthesis (L8040, L8041, L8042, L8043, L8044, L8045, L8046, L8047) describe a complete prosthesis":
an item is a facial prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L8040", "L8041", "L8042", "L8043", "L8044", "L8045", "L8046", "L8047"].

rule facial_prosthesis_unspecified with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "If a facial prosthesis is not described by a specific code, L8040, L8041, L8042, L8043, L8044, L8045, L8046, or L8047":
an item is a facial prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L8048"
    and the kind of the item is unspecified facial prosthesis.

% A prosthesis that is itself covered for its beneficiary, and an item used
% with one or a service on one. Devices of this model.
rule facial_covered_prosthesis:
an item is a covered facial prosthesis for a beneficiary
    if the item is a facial prosthesis
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a qualifying facial condition.

rule facial_used_with:
an item is used with a covered facial prosthesis
    if the item is an accessory of a device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the device is a covered facial prosthesis for the beneficiary.

rule facial_service_on:
an item is a repair or modification of a covered facial prosthesis
    if the item is an accessory of a device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the device is a covered facial prosthesis for the beneficiary.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides: the prostheses, the miscellaneous code and
% the labor code, the adhesives and tape, and the skin care products the
% Article denies; the benefit — the statutory benefit of Social Security
% Act §1861(s)(9) — is not the skin care products'.
rule facial_codes with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Adhesives, adhesive remover, and tape used in conjunction with a facial prosthesis should be billed using codes A4364, A4455, A4456, A4450, or A4452":
the policy for code a code is facial_prostheses
    if the code is in ["L8040", "L8041", "L8042", "L8043", "L8044", "L8045", "L8046", "L8047", "L8048", "L8049", "A4364", "A4455", "A4456", "A4450", "A4452", "A5120", "A9270"].

section applicability is:

rule facial_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Facial prostheses are covered under the Medicare Artificial Legs, Arms and Eyes benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the benefit category of code a code is "artificial legs, arms and eyes"
    if the policy for code the code is facial_prostheses
    and it is not the case that
        the code is "A9270".

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The claims: a prosthesis, its replacement, the supplies used with it, its
% repair or modification.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule facial_covered with provenance LCD L33738,
        confer "A facial prosthesis is covered when there is loss or absence of facial tissue due to disease, trauma, surgery, or a congenital defect":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is a covered facial prosthesis for the beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the item replaces a previous facial prosthesis.

rule facial_replacement with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Replacement of a facial prosthesis is covered in cases of loss or irreparable damage or wear or when required because of a change in the beneficiary’s condition that cannot be accommodated by modification of the existing prosthesis":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is a covered facial prosthesis for the beneficiary
    and the item replaces a previous facial prosthesis
    and the finding replacement justified about the beneficiary is established.

rule facial_supplies with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Adhesives, adhesive remover, skin barrier wipes, and tape used in conjunction with a facial prosthesis are covered":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4364", "A4455", "A4456", "A4450", "A4452", "A5120"]
    and the item is used with a covered facial prosthesis.

rule facial_attachment with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "If a facial prosthesis has a component which is used to attach it to a bone-anchored implant or to an internal prosthesis (e.g., maxillary obturator), that component should be billed separately using code L8048":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "L8048"
    and the kind of the item is attachment component
    and the item is used with a covered facial prosthesis.

rule facial_repair with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Repairs are covered when there has been accidental damage or extensive wear to the prosthesis that can be repaired":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L8048", "L8049"]
    and the item is a repair or modification of a covered facial prosthesis
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the item repairs accidental damage or extensive wear to the device.

rule facial_modification with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Modifications to a prosthesis are separately payable when they occur more than 90 days after delivery of the prosthesis and they are required because of a change in the beneficiary’s condition":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L8048", "L8049"]
    and the item is a repair or modification of a covered facial prosthesis
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the item is a modification made more than 90 days after the delivery of the device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding change in condition requires modification about the beneficiary is established.

% A modification within 90 days of delivery is in the allowance of the
% prosthesis.
rule facial_modification_timing with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Modifications to the prosthesis made at the time delivery of the prosthesis or within 90 days thereafter":
an item is a modification made more than 90 days after the delivery of a device
    if a claim is for the item
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the device was delivered on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number > 90.

% Criterion 1: the condition and its cause.
rule facial_condition with provenance LCD L33738,
        confer "loss or absence of facial tissue due to disease, trauma, surgery, or a congenital defect":
a beneficiary has a qualifying facial condition
    if the beneficiary has a condition of facial tissue due to a cause
    and the condition is in [loss, absence]
    and the cause is in [disease, trauma, surgery, congenital defect].

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment (Policy Article A52463, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements").
rule facial_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "When either code V2629 or L8048 is billed, the claim must be accompanied by a brief description of the item in the narrative field":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is facial_prostheses
    and the claim is for an item
    and the narrative description requirement is met for the item
    and the photograph requirement is met for the item
    and the new impression requirement is met for the item.

rule facial_narrative with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "When either code V2629 or L8048 is billed, the claim must be accompanied by a brief description of the item in the narrative field":
the narrative description requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L8048"
    and the claim for the item includes a description of the item in the narrative field.

rule facial_no_narrative with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "When either code V2629 or L8048 is billed, the claim must be accompanied by a brief description of the item in the narrative field":
the narrative description requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is "L8048".

rule facial_photograph with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "When L8048 is provided, a drawing/photograph of the item provided must be available upon request":
the photograph requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L8048"
    and a drawing or photograph of the item is available.

rule facial_no_photograph with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "When L8048 is provided, a drawing/photograph of the item provided must be available upon request":
the photograph requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is "L8048".

rule facial_new_impression with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "When replacement involves a new impression/moulage rather than use of a previous master model, the reason for the new impression/moulage must be clearly documented in the supplier's records and available upon request":
the new impression requirement is met for an item
    if the item was fabricated from a new impression
    and the reason for the new impression for the item is documented in the supplier records.

rule facial_previous_model with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "When replacement involves a new impression/moulage rather than use of a previous master model, the reason for the new impression/moulage must be clearly documented in the supplier's records and available upon request":
the new impression requirement is met for an item
    if the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the item was fabricated from a new impression.
